{
  "$comment": [
    "SHARED CITATION-PARITY CORPUS — executed by BOTH resolvers (#699, 2026-09-01).",
    "",
    "WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `composeCitationResolver.ts` is a hand-written client mirror of the server",
    "`CitationResolver.cs`. Both had parity test cases, but they were TRANSCRIBED by hand into two",
    "suites — so the two parsers could drift and both suites would stay green, because each only ever",
    "asserted against its own copy of the expectations. This corpus is the single set of expectations;",
    "each side runs it against its own parser, so a divergence fails on the side that lags.",
    "",
    "WHY DIVERGENCE MATTERS FOR #699. When the client cannot parse a citation the server can, the",
    "deterministic anchor leg in `placeAdvisoryComments` returns null and the finding falls through to",
    "TEXT search — reinstating exactly the wrong-clause anchoring #699 is about. A silent parser gap is",
    "therefore not a cosmetic inconsistency; it is the defect coming back through a side door.",
    "",
    "MAINTENANCE. Adding a citation SHAPE to either parser means adding a case here. The vocabulary/",
    "shape-enum drift detector that makes forgetting hard is",
    "tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/ComposeCitationResolverParityGuardTests.cs.",
    "",
    "`paraIds` is the EXPECTED match list in document order (empty = an explicit not-found, which is a",
    "valid answer and never a fabricated paraId). `shape` is the parse classification both sides must",
    "agree on independently of what matched."
  ],

